# .no-backup — gitignored paths that deliberately have no backup, and WHY.
# Read by hygiene-check.py. Anything ignored and NOT listed here gets reported.
# One path prefix per line, then the reason. A reason is the point: "it is noisy" is not one.
#
# Also supports:  BACKED-UP  <path>  <YYYY-MM-DD>  <where>   for paths that ARE copied by hand.

CLAUDE.md      ⚠️ NOT regenerable, and this is an accepted loss rather than a safe one (Ethan's
               call, 2026-08-06). It is held out of the repo via .git/info/exclude because this is
               a public repo with no private twin, so there is nowhere tracked to keep it. It is
               the only copy of this project's private context and its publishing rules. If it is
               lost, those are lost with it and the next session will not know to apply them. The
               clean fix is a minimal private twin to hold it; that was declined for now.
.env.local     holds Vercel credentials (a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN and project linkage). Credentials do
               not go on an unencrypted stick that travels — Set A rule 1, Set C rule C5. This is
               deliberately unrecoverable: regenerate it with `vercel env pull`, which is the whole
               reason it must not be backed up rather than a gap in the backups.
.build/        test and build output, regenerated by `npm run build` / the test run.
public/maplibre/   MapLibre's worker and shared bundles, copied out of node_modules at build time
               so they are served same-origin. Vendored output, not source: `npm ci` plus the
               copy step reproduces them exactly.
test-results/  Playwright run output, regenerated by the e2e suite.
